-- title:
--   Descent from $\mathbb{R}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{R}$ to $F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$ through a basis and an $F$-linear functional
-- statement:
--   This file constructs a $\mathbb{Q}$-linear map that pushes elements of $\mathbb{R}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{R}$ down to $F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$ for a subfield $F$ of $\mathbb{R}$.
--
--   Let $F$ be an intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}\subseteq F\subseteq\mathbb{R}$ and regard $\mathbb{R}$ as a vector space over $F$. Fix an $F$-basis $(b_k)_{k\in\iota}$ of $\mathbb{R}$, indexed by an arbitrary set $\iota$, so that every $x\in\mathbb{R}$ has a unique expansion $x=\sum_k x_kb_k$ with coordinates $x_k\in F$, only finitely many of them nonzero. Fix also an $F$-linear map $\varphi:\mathbb{R}\to F$. All tensor products are over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$ is regarded as a commutative ring.
--
--   1. **Tensor coordinates.** Tensoring the coordinate isomorphism $\mathbb{R}\cong\bigoplus_{k\in\iota}F$ (viewed over $\mathbb{Q}$) with itself gives the $\mathbb{Q}$-linear isomorphism
--   $$\kappa:\ \mathbb{R}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{R}\ \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\ \bigoplus_{(k,l)\in\iota\times\iota}F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F,\qquad \kappa(x\otimes y)_{(k,l)}=x_k\otimes y_l ,$$
--   whose target consists of the finitely supported families indexed by $\iota\times\iota$.
--   2. **Coefficient trace.** The $F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$-linear map from finitely supported families to $F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$ given by
--   $$\tau\bigl((z_{kl})_{(k,l)}\bigr)=\sum_{(k,l)\in\iota\times\iota}z_{kl}\,\bigl(\varphi(b_kb_l)\otimes1\bigr).$$
--   3. **Tensor descent.** The $\mathbb{Q}$-linear map $\delta=\tau\circ\kappa:\mathbb{R}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{R}\to F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$. On pure tensors,
--   $$\delta(x\otimes y)=\sum_{k,l\in\iota}x_k\,\varphi(b_kb_l)\otimes y_l .$$
--
--   The descent map is the bridge from real coefficients to coefficients in a subfield. It is compatible with two-sided multiplication by elements of $F$, namely $\delta\bigl((x\otimes1)\,t\,(1\otimes y)\bigr)=(x\otimes1)\,\delta(t)\,(1\otimes y)$ for $x,y\in F$ and $t\in\mathbb{R}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{R}$, and with the multiplication maps, $m_F(\delta(t))=\varphi(m(t))$, where $m$ and $m_F$ send $x\otimes y$ to $xy$. Taking for $F$ the field generated by the coordinates of a point configuration and for $\varphi$ an $F$-linear functional with $\varphi(1)=1$, applying $\delta$ entrywise therefore turns a solution of the real tensor criterion (with entries in $\mathbb{R}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{R}$) into a solution of the field criterion (with entries in $F\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}F$).
--
--   **Formalization Note** `tensorCoordinates F b` is assembled from `b.repr.restrictScalars ℚ` (via `TensorProduct.congr`) and `finsuppTensorFinsupp`, and takes values in `ι × ι →₀ (F ⊗[ℚ] F)`; `coefficientTrace F b φ` is a `Finsupp.linearCombination`; `tensorDescent F b φ` is their composite, with scalars restricted to $\mathbb{Q}$. `tensorRing` is a local instance providing the commutative ring structure on `F ⊗[ℚ] F`. The two compatibility properties quoted above are proved separately, not in this file; a compatibility section at the top of the file is empty.
